# Auto-generated by the AutoML pipeline. Default-deny build context -- see the rules below.
# --- AutoML default-deny allow-list (v4) ---
# [RULE 1] The Dockerfile does ONE `COPY . ./`; THIS file decides what is in the build context. Default-deny: everything is ignored
# unless it is listed below, and the exclusions at the very end win (last matching rule wins), so no model type needs a hand-made file
# list and a model file added after the Dockerfile was generated is still copied.
# [STRUCTURED-LAYOUT FIX] This file must sit at the REPOSITORY ROOT (the Docker build context): `docker build -f deployment/Dockerfile .`
# ignores a .dockerignore nested in deployment/. Flat bundles (app.py at the root) and structured ones (src/ config/ artifacts/) both work.
*
# --- serving code (flat layout) ---
!app.py
!requirements.txt
# --- model / preprocessing / config formats at the root (flat layout) ---
